gher priority —\n    /// `src/state/priority-formula.mjs`'s inverted scale). `None` when the\n    /// item never had `computePriority` run on it yet (e.g. still at\n    /// `todo`, pre-`discover`).\n    pub priority: Option<i64>,\n}","target":"docs/knowledge/fgos-triage-table-columns/triage-table-columns.md","targetCommit":"dc24ce64527fbffd23e1643f35a7ddf808fd7b45","targetDigest":"4911e8f2a96eb1af83e107184211d9ad3e02a74f082ff45fe9e9907c67d87e5d","targetEvidence":[{"line":20,"text":"| `status` | `status` | raw status (`todo` \\| `doing` \\| `blocked` \\| `awaiting-approval` \\| `delivered` \\| `retrospective` \\| `cleanup` \\| `done` \\| `awaiting-human` \\| `wontfix`), rendered as-is |"}],"comparisons":{"counts":{"verdict":"not-asserted","note":"The renamed reference explicitly says raw status is rendered as-is. This proves the raw-literal field claim, without adding any status/column behavior."},"ports":{"verdict":"not-asserted","note":"The renamed reference explicitly says raw status is rendered as-is. This proves the raw-literal field claim, without adding any status/column behavior."},"defaults":{"verdict":"not-asserted","note":"The renamed reference explicitly says raw status is rendered as-is. This proves the raw-literal field claim, without adding any status/column behavior."},"verbFileLists":{"verdict":"not-asserted","note":"The renamed reference explicitly says raw status is rendered as-is. This proves the raw-literal field claim, without adding any status/column behavior."},"versions":{"verdict":"not-asserted","note":"The renamed reference explicitly says raw status is rendered as-is. This proves the raw-literal field claim, without adding any status/column behavior."},"shippedStatus":{"verdict":"not-asserted","note":"The renamed reference explicitly says raw status is rendered as-is. This proves the raw-literal field claim, without adding any status/column behavior."}},"assessment":"The renamed reference explicitly says raw status is rendered as-is. This proves the raw-literal field claim, without adding any status/column behavior."},"{\"edgeId\":\"class6-l-000201\",\"file\":\"packages/herdr-fgos-common/rust/src/fgos.rs\",\"inventoryRefs\":[{\"edgeId\":\"class6-l-000201\",\"inputCommit\":\"42edba2b08d26ab8dcabe4859a301e1589fa8e6b\",\"inventory\":\"step-02l-census-class6.json\",\"originalLine\":242}]}":{"sourcePassage":"/// absent-sorts-last convention `docs/reference/triage-table-columns.md`","adjacentPassage":"/// Parse `fgos triage --json`'s stdout. tsk-64z D2: re-sorts by `priority`\n/// ASCENDING (`priority-formula.mjs`'s inverted scale — smaller number =\n/// higher priority), overriding `rankImpact`'s own default tier/blocks/\n/// component order (the order tsk-4vo originally asked to preserve\n/// byte-for-byte — see `parse_triage_preserves_rank_impact_order`, still\n/// pinned for the CLI's own `--all`-less order, just no longer what this\n/// function returns). An absent `priority` (`None` — an item that never\n/// had `computePriority` run, e.g. still at `todo`) sorts LAST, same\n/// absent-sorts-last convention `docs/reference/triage-table-columns.md`\n/// already documents for `goalTier`.\npub fn parse_triage(json: &str) -> Result<Vec<TriageRow>, serde_json::Error> {\n    let envelope: TriageEnvelope = serde_json::from_str(json)?;\n    let mut rows = envelope.data;\n    rows.sort_by_key(|row| row.priority.unwrap_or(i64::MAX));\n    Ok(rows)\n}","target":"docs/knowledge/fgos-triage-table-columns/triage-table-columns.md","targetCommit":"dc24ce64527fbffd23e1643f35a7ddf808fd7b45","targetDigest":"4911e8f2a96eb1af83e107184211d9ad3e02a74f082ff45fe9e9907c67d87e5d","targetEvidence":[{"line":1,"text":"---"}],"comparisons":{"counts":{"verdict":"not-asserted","note":"L12-62: Same-basename moved-verbatim knowledge holder; complete historical source text conserved. Ruling 1 permits this Phase 9 repair."},"ports":{"verdict":"not-asserted","note":"L12-62: Same-basename moved-verbatim knowledge holder; complete historica